<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Aref Bourhan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Aref Bourhan was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> politician who headed the government council of the French Territory of the Afars and the Issas, present-day Djibouti, from 1967 to 1976. He favoured continued ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and his fall preceded the territory's independence as the Republic of Djibouti in 1977.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-aref-bourhan.jpg" alt="Ali Aref Bourhan" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: André Cros · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:14.5.71._R%C3%A9gine_Soul%C3%A9_et_Ali_Aref_la_veille_de_leur_fian%C3%A7ailles_%C3%A0_Carcassonne_(1971)_-_53Fi5639_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
